      "location": "4.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 4.1 defines “F_N(δ)=H(p_NN,s_Np_NN+δ)+H(q_NN,s_Nq_NN−δ)−H(s_NN,s_Np_NN+δ)−(s_Np_NN+δ)log p_N−(s_Nq_NN−δ)log q_N” and then says Taylor's formula gives the finite expansion for log L_N(B_N). As defined, F_N(0)=N H(s_N); the full log likelihood ratio also contains the constant entropy term −H(N,s_NN)=−N H(s_N), which is not included in F_N or explicitly canceled in the Taylor step. The preceding cancellation observation makes this a short algebra repair, but the displayed expansion does not explicitly perform it.",
